# upstream-candidates/dma-buf-compressed-descriptor/README.md). Adds an
# optional {codec, block_size, uncompressed_size} descriptor so an exporter
# that has compressed a buffer's contents in place (rather than evicting and
# later re-fetching them) can tell an importer how to inflate it. Same 3
# files as 0019. New ioctls are numbered 6/7, not 4/5, since 0019 already
# claims those.
#
# Authored as a real git commit ON TOP OF 0019 (not against the clean base)
# — an earlier draft authored against the clean base looked like it had
# non-overlapping hunks by inspection, but `git am --3way` for the real
# 0001-0020 sequence hit 3 conflicts (dma-buf.c, both headers) because 0019's
# inserted lines shifted every anchor. Re-authored directly on a tree with
# 0001-0019 already applied, verified 2026-08-10 via an actual (not merely
# planned) sequential `git am --3way` of the full 18-patch series against a
# fresh 7.1.8 kernel-org clone — 0 conflicts, then confirmed
# drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.o and drivers/gpu/drm/drm_prime.o both build clean
